<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">15 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 15 March, from 200 BCE to 2019.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/galba" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/galba.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">200 BCE <span class="tih-ago">2,225 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sulpicius Galba and Aurelius Cotta become consuls in Rome</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Publius Sulpicius <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galba">Galba</a> and Gaius Aurelius Cotta took office as consuls in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. Sulpicius, charged with Macedonia, persuaded the Comitia centuriata at a second session to vote for war on Philip V, beginning the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-macedonian-war">Second Macedonian War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-macedonian-war">Second Macedonian War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-v-of-macedon">Philip V of Macedon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/44-bce">44 BCE</a> <span class="tih-ago">2,069 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Julius Caesar assassinated on the Ides of March</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A group of senators led by Brutus and Cassius stabbed Caesar to death in the Curia of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a>. Meant to save the Republic, the murder led to civil war and the rule of Augustus.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">493 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,533 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Theoderic the Great kills Odoacer at Ravenna</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a long siege ended in a power-sharing agreement, Theoderic murdered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a> at a banquet. The Ostrogothic king then ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> for over thirty years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">933 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,093 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry the Fowler defeats the Magyars at Riade</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-fowler">Henry the Fowler</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-francia">East Francia</a> routed a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magyars">Magyar</a> army near the river <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unstrut">Unstrut</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>, after refusing to pay further tribute. The victory raised the prestige of the Saxon dynasty, though Magyar raids continued until 955.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-riade">Battle of Riade</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-fowler">Henry the Fowler</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1493">1493 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">533 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Columbus returns to Spain from his first voyage</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Columbus</a> sailed into Palos, the port from which he had departed seven months earlier, with news of islands across the Atlantic. His voyages began lasting European contact with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1564">1564 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">462 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Akbar abolishes the jizya tax on non-Muslims</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Mughal emperor ended the poll tax on non-Muslim subjects, part of a policy of conciliating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> majority of his empire. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a> reimposed it in 1679.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1820">1820 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">206 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Maine becomes the 23rd US state</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Separated from Massachusetts, Maine entered the Union as a free state under the Missouri Compromise. Its admission balanced that of Missouri as a slave state.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1917">1917 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">109 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tsar Nicholas II abdicates</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Facing revolution in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a> and mutiny in the army, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii">Nicholas II</a> gave up the throne for himself and his son. Over three centuries of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-romanov">Romanov</a> rule ended, and a Provisional Government took power.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii">Nicholas II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2019">2019 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">7 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gunman kills 51 at two Christchurch mosques</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A white supremacist attacked worshippers at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khutba">Friday prayers</a> and livestreamed the killings. Within a month <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a>'s parliament banned most semi-automatic weapons.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a></div></div></li></ol>
